#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`bun run cat regen`: every check/writer pair the CI workflow runs, repeated until the tree settles."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:110
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`git merge --abort`. Each refused path is listed with its pattern's reason, or \"no declared pattern\"."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`git merge --no-ff --no-commit origin/main` on a clean tree (untracked files refuse too, so the final stage cannot sweep in a scratch file)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:135
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`new` on three conditions and no others: a failure whose signature the PR's own comment did not already report; a member that reported no verdict, or one it could not classify; and a systemic failure (every selected PR failed) unless every one of those failures is itself a repeat, in which case each PR's comment already reports its own condition and the run that made it true was the loud one. A repeat of an identical failure on an unchanged head is `already reported`."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`no` if even one path is refused: the merge is aborted whole, never half-resolved."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`no` when regen reports an unrepaired check, or one with no writer: a resolution the gates cannot reproduce is not a resolution."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`none` still regenerates: a CLEAN merge can produce an artefact neither side would emit (bean `lxpq`), so only the gates can say it is right."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn:125
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A SECOND trigger, not a step of the merge above: `merge-main.yml` runs one merge per opted-in PR and this fires once per RUN, when all of them have reported. Drawn separately because a diagram that showed it inside one PR's flow would say the run notifies per PR, which is the defect it exists to fix (bean `03nl`)."
msgstr ""

